# Bench-only fragment. NEVER part of a release.
#
# It adds two exceptions to the product profile, and each is a named symbol
# rather than a quiet default because the record of which safety evidence a
# build went without is the entire point of having it:
#
#   HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_PROFILE   No G0/G2 driver-protection profile exists
#                                    and the gate that keeps the amplifiers
#                                    muted for that reason is lifted anyway.
#   HK_BENCH_PROVISIONAL_PROFILE     The DSP chain runs on a compiled-in
#                                    profile nobody measured, in place of the
#                                    crossover corner, protective high-pass
#                                    corner and limiter ceilings G0/G2 will
#                                    produce.
#
# THIS RELEASES THE AMPLIFIERS. hk_audio_hw drives HK_PIN_DAC_XSMT, the only
# mute in the chain: the XH-A232 boards have no mute or shutdown input and are
# live from the moment the 24 V rail is. With the first symbol set the DAC is
# unmuted, and a DAC on the I2S pins feeding four always-on amplifiers means
# AirPlay audio reaches whatever is wired to their outputs, with nothing in
# front of it but numbers nobody measured.
#
# So the standard for "defensible" is narrow. This is defensible into a dummy
# load, into a scope, or into nothing at all. It is NOT defensible into the Nova
# drivers: their impedance curve is still the open G0 blocker, and without it
# there is no informed limit on what the amplifiers may be asked to produce.
# Look at what is connected to the speaker terminals before you flash a build
# made from this file.
#
# Build with it:
#   idf.py -C firmware -B firmware/build-bench \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.bench" \
#     -D SDKCONFIG="$PWD/firmware/build-bench/sdkconfig" build
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_PROFILE=y

# Lets the DSP chain run without a manufactured calibration. Two of its numbers
# are measured (the DC resistances); the rest are reasoned. See the Kconfig help.
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_PROVISIONAL_PROFILE=y

# The DSP output backend: mono downmix, EQ, subsonic, LR4 crossover into the two
# DAC channels, each paralleled into four amplifiers, and a per-branch limiter
# last. Left = woofer, right = tweeter, which is the bi-amp mapping ADR-0002
# fixed.
CONFIG_HK_AIRPLAY_OUTPUT_DSP=y

# NOT set: the bench board's crossed leads were fixed in the harness instead.
# The switch stays in the tree because the failure it catches is real and was
# found here -- with a mono programme a crossed pair is completely invisible,
# and it only announces itself by putting bass into a tweeter the first time a
# crossover works. The DAC's two lines are paralleled into four amplifier inputs
# by hand.
# CONFIG_HK_OUTPUT_SWAP_BRANCHES is not set
